{"name":"Anchor Grey","hex":"#596062","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"anchor","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tool used to moor a vessel to the bottom of a sea or river to resist movement.","An iron device so shaped as to grip the bottom and hold a vessel at her berth by the chain or rope attached."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To connect an object, especially a ship or a boat, to a fixed point.","To cast anchor; to come to anchor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anchor"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Anchor","blocks":[{"text":"An anchor is a device, normally made of metal, used to secure a vessel to the bed of a body of water to prevent the craft from drifting due to wind or current. The word derives from Latin ancora, which itself comes from the Greek ἄγκυρα."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Kotwica_SS_Pozna%C5%84.JPG/330px-Kotwica_SS_Pozna%C5%84.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anchor"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Amoco_Cadiz_anchor.jpg/500px-Amoco_Cadiz_an